## Do NOT say / do on camera
- Don't say "you need Calico" — CNI is only needed for NetworkPolicy. [D]
- Don't say quarantine leaves the network alone — on 1.4 it blocks outbound too. [D]
- Don't say the gateway blocks a shadow — shadows get the kernel lockdown only. [D]
- Don't name or criticise other vendors' gateways — compare with "a gateway alone".
- Don't run a live install (too slow) — show the result.
- Don't use `fileSystem` in a sandbox policy if you'll `exec` afterwards. [C]
- Don't ask Calico questions in the bank chat. [C]
- Don't demo or imply 1.5 features run on this cluster (it's 1.4.2). Don't say 1.5's new file rules fix the exec problem — the notes don't say that. [RN]
